assets/raw/*
# The pattern is `assets/raw/*` and not `assets/raw/` for one mechanical reason:
# git does not descend into an ignored DIRECTORY at all, so a file-level
# exception inside one is silently inert. Excluding the CONTENTS keeps the
# directory walkable and makes the negation at the bottom real.
#
# EXCEPTION below, and the reason it is needed: a frame listed in
# tools/atlas-sizes.json `extractStandalone` is RE-ENCODED FROM assets/raw/ into
# assets/<name>.png on every `pack-atlas` run. For those frames the file under
# assets/ is a build OUTPUT, and the raw source is the input that decides it.
#
# Iteration 79 shipped the consequence of ignoring that. The title art was
# regenerated by hand directly into assets/ui-title-art.png (a build artifact),
# assets/raw/ui-title-art.png was left holding the old plate, and the next repack
# — run to integrate four unrelated facility markers — silently reverted the fix:
# 270,524 pixels, 26% of the screen, back to the art two iterations had been
# spent replacing. A green suite, a clean build and a passing capture gate all
# straight through it, because nothing in the repo claimed the two files were
# related.
#
# So the SOURCE of a standalone frame is committed. Everything else in
# assets/raw/ stays ignored, because everything else in there is reproducible by
# re-running the generator and the packed atlas is what ships.
# tests/unit/atlas.test.ts enforces both halves of this.
!assets/raw/ui-title-art.png
# Generated source art staged by tools/gen-codex-assets.mjs before
# tools/integrate-codex-assets.mjs folds it into assets/raw/ and repacks the
# atlas. Same category as assets/raw/: reproducible from the generator, and the
# packed atlas is what ships.
assets/raw-codex/
# Visual-review captures from tools/shoot.mjs. Local evidence, tens of MB.
.shots/
.remember/
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/

# The reviewer runs from an isolated HOME (tools/review-codex.sh) so the user's
# 537-skill context library does not load into every call. Its session logs are
# 100MB+ each and are never worth committing.
.opencode/codex-home/
